---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Desire Resorts Suites & Room Selection Guide
description: "Browse every suite type at Desire Riviera Maya and Desire Pearl, across current room and suite categories, with amenities and room-selection notes."
permalink: '/rooms/'
---

<article class="rooms-editorial page container">
  <header class="rooms-header text-center">
    <span class="hero-eyebrow">Accommodations & Layouts</span>
    <h1>Find Your Sanctuary</h1>
    <p class="hero-lead" style="max-width: var(--max-paragraph); margin: 0 auto 28px; color: var(--color-espresso-soft);">
      Room choice is easier when you separate the things that actually change: view, private water features, living space, service level, and location. Use this page to compare current categories without treating any one room as a universal best choice.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="independent-guide-banner room-guide-note" role="note"><strong>Independent room guide:</strong> Category names, features, locations, inclusions, and availability can change. These descriptions are planning guidance based on currently listed room information. Confirm the exact category and current inclusions with the resort or booking channel before paying a premium for an upgrade.</div>

  <!-- Concierge Room Selection Advice -->
  <div class="verdict-banner text-center" style="max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto 40px;">
    <h3>Concierge Room Placement Tip</h3>
    <p>
      If room location matters to you, compare the current category, view, and proximity to the areas you expect to use most. Room names, locations, features, and availability can change, so confirm the current details before booking.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- The Eden Explainer -->
  <div class="verdict-banner text-center" style="max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto 40px;">
    <h3>What Is The Eden?</h3>
    <p>
      The Eden is a distinct accommodation section within Riviera Maya, with its own suite categories (Beloved, Seductive Swim-Up, and Diamond Ocean-View, marked below), rather than a rebrand of existing rooms. The Eden is presented here as its own room tier within Riviera Maya rather than as a replacement for the resort's other categories. Compare the exact room category, listed amenities, and current access or service details before booking.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="room-selection-checklist" aria-labelledby="room-selection-heading">
    <div><span class="section-eyebrow">Before You Upgrade</span><h2 id="room-selection-heading">Five Questions to Ask</h2></div>
    <ol class="room-selection-checklist__grid">
      <li><strong>What view do we actually want?</strong><span>Garden, tropical, pool, ocean, or oceanfront can be a bigger difference than an amenity you may rarely use.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Do we want private water?</strong><span>Separate a jacuzzi, plunge pool, and swim-up connection. They are not interchangeable.</span></li>
      <li><strong>How much living space matters?</strong><span>Look at the layout, not just the word “suite.” Categories vary in living areas, bathrooms, terraces, and levels.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Which services matter?</strong><span>Check whether the category currently lists butler service, transfers, VIP check-in, dining privileges, or other extras.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Where will we spend our time?</strong><span>Ask about the room's location and nearby areas if proximity matters. A category name alone does not tell you the exact building.</span></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <!-- How to compare room categories -->
  <section class="room-difference-guide" aria-labelledby="room-difference-heading">
    <div class="room-difference-guide__intro">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">How to Compare</span>
      <h2 id="room-difference-heading">Start With What Matters Most to You</h2>
      <p>Room categories are easier to compare when you separate the upgrades into four questions: <strong>What do you want to see?</strong> <strong>How much private space do you want?</strong> <strong>Do you want a private water feature?</strong> And <strong>how much extra service matters?</strong></p>
    </div>
    <div class="room-difference-guide__grid">
      <div class="room-difference-guide__item"><strong>View</strong><span>Garden, Relax Pool, main pool, or oceanfront can change the feel of your room more than a small amenity upgrade.</span></div>
      <div class="room-difference-guide__item"><strong>Space</strong><span>Moving from a standard room to a suite can add living areas, dining space, multiple bathrooms, or a two-level layout.</span></div>
      <div class="room-difference-guide__item"><strong>Private water</strong><span>Jacuzzis, plunge pools, and swim-up access are different experiences. Decide which one you actually want before paying for the upgrade.</span></div>
      <div class="room-difference-guide__item"><strong>Service</strong><span>Higher categories can add features such as butler service, airport transfers, VIP check-in, premium bars, or other listed extras.</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="room-difference-guide__note">These are comparison principles, not guarantees of a particular building or location. Room names, features, inclusions, and availability can change.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Resort-level comparison -->
  <section class="room-category-summary" aria-labelledby="room-category-summary-heading">
    <div class="room-category-summary__intro">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Quick Reference</span>
      <h2 id="room-category-summary-heading">Where the Major Upgrades Happen</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="room-category-summary__table-wrap">
      <table class="room-category-summary__table">
        <caption class="sr-only">Major room-category differences at Desire Riviera Maya and Desire Pearl</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">If you care most about...</th><th scope="col">Look first at...</th><th scope="col">What changes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">A better view</th><td>Deluxe Ocean, Jacuzzi Ocean, Oceanfront, or Diamond Ocean-View</td><td>The outlook becomes the main upgrade.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">A private jacuzzi</th><td>Jacuzzi Rooms, Eden Jacuzzi Suites, Mansion Jacuzzi</td><td>You add a dedicated private soaking space.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Swim-up access</th><td>Eden Swim-Up, Desire Suites, Mansion Swim-Up</td><td>Your room connects directly to a pool.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">More living space</th><td>Junior, Master, Mansion, Desire, Penthouse</td><td>You move into a larger suite layout.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Premium service</th><td>Heavenly, Oceanfront, Desire, Diamond, Mansion</td><td>More categories include butler, transfer, VIP, or other premium services.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Interactive Segmented Filters -->
  <div class="room-filter-container text-center">
    <div class="filter-group">
      <span class="filter-label">Resort:</span>
      <div class="filter-pills" id="property-pills" role="group" aria-label="Filter by resort">
        <button type="button" class="room-pill is-active" aria-pressed="true" data-property="all">All Properties</button>
        <button type="button" class="room-pill" aria-pressed="false" data-property="drm">Desire Riviera Maya</button>
        <button type="button" class="room-pill" aria-pressed="false" data-property="pearl">Desire Pearl</button>
      </div>
      <span id="room-property-status" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Showing rooms at all properties.</span>
    </div>

    <div class="filter-group" style="margin-top: 16px;">
      <span class="filter-label">Private water:</span>
      <div class="filter-pills" id="vibe-pills" role="group" aria-label="Filter by private water feature">
        <button type="button" class="room-pill is-active" aria-pressed="true" data-vibe="all">All Rooms</button>
        <button type="button" class="room-pill" aria-pressed="false" data-vibe="private-water">Jacuzzi / Plunge Pool</button>
        <button type="button" class="room-pill" aria-pressed="false" data-vibe="swim-up">Swim-Up</button>
      </div>
      <span id="room-vibe-status" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Showing all room categories.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Room Cards Grid -->
  <div id="room-grid" class="rooms-cards-grid grid-auto-lg">
    {% for room in collections.room %}
      <article class="suite-card" data-property="{{ room.data.property }}" data-feature="{% set roomTitle = room.data.title | lower %}{% if "swim-up" in roomTitle %}swim-up{% elif "jacuzzi" in roomTitle or "plunge" in roomTitle or "whirlpool" in roomTitle %}private-water{% else %}standard{% endif %}">
        <div class="suite-card__top">
          <span class="property-tag">
            {{ 'Riviera Maya' if room.data.property == 'drm' else 'Pearl' }}
          </span>
          <span class="vibe-badge {{ 'is-party' if room.data.vibe == 'heart-of-the-party' else 'is-quiet' }}">
            {{ 'Swim-Up / Water Access' if room.data.vibe == 'heart-of-the-party' else 'Jacuzzi / Plunge Pool' }}
          </span>
        </div>

        <div class="suite-card__header">
          <h3>{{ room.data.title }}</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="suite-card__body">
          <div class="suite-difference"><span class="suite-difference__label">Main difference</span><strong>{{ room.data.difference }}</strong></div>
          {{ room.templateContent | safe }}
        </div>

        {% if room.data.amenities %}
          <div class="suite-amenities">
            <span class="amenity-title">Typical Features:</span>
            <ul class="amenity-tags">
              {% for amenity in room.data.amenities %}
                <li>{{ amenity }}</li>
              {% endfor %}
            </ul>
            <p class="small-text" style="color: var(--color-espresso-soft); margin-top: 8px;">Features listed are typical for this room category and can change&mdash;confirm current inclusions with the resort before booking.</p>
          </div>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="suite-card__footer">
          <a href="/#availability" class="btn btn--primary" style="width: 100%;">Check Suite Availability</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <!-- Concierge Reassurance Footer -->
  <section class="concierge-trust-banner text-center" style="margin-top: 60px;">
    <h3>Need Help Selecting the Right Building?</h3>
    <p style="color: var(--color-espresso-soft); max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 20px;">
      Specific room categories differ in views, layouts, water features, service, and location. Start with the characteristic that matters most to you, then confirm the exact category before booking.
    </p>
    <a href="/quiz/" class="btn btn--outline">Take the 60-Second Planning Quiz &rarr;</a>
  </section>
</article>


  <section class="first-timer-next-step" aria-labelledby="first-timer-next-heading">
    <div class="first-timer-next-step__content">
      <span class="ft-card__label">04</span>
      <h2 id="first-timer-next-heading">Next: Picture Your First Day</h2>
      <p>Once you have a room category in mind, see how a typical day can flow from arrival and breakfast through pool time, dinner, and the evening.</p>
    </div>
    <a href="/day-in-the-life/" class="editorial-btn editorial-btn--outline">See a Day at Desire &rarr;</a>
  </section>

<script>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const propPills = document.querySelectorAll('#property-pills .room-pill');
    const vibePills = document.querySelectorAll('#vibe-pills .room-pill');
    const cards = document.querySelectorAll('.suite-card');

    let activeProp = 'all';
    let activeVibe = 'all';

    function filterSuites() {
      cards.forEach(card => {
        const matchProp = (activeProp === 'all' || card.dataset.property === activeProp);
        const matchVibe = (activeVibe === 'all' || card.dataset.feature === activeVibe);

        if (matchProp && matchVibe) {
          card.style.display = 'flex';
        } else {
          card.style.display = 'none';
        }
      });
    }

    propPills.forEach(pill => {
      pill.addEventListener('click', () => {
        propPills.forEach(p => { p.classList.remove('is-active'); p.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false'); });
        pill.classList.add('is-active');
        pill.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');
        activeProp = pill.dataset.property;
        const status = document.getElementById('room-property-status');
        if (status) status.textContent = `Showing rooms at ${pill.textContent.trim().toLowerCase()}.`;
        filterSuites();
      });
    });

    vibePills.forEach(pill => {
      pill.addEventListener('click', () => {
        vibePills.forEach(p => { p.classList.remove('is-active'); p.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false'); });
        pill.classList.add('is-active');
        pill.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');
        activeVibe = pill.dataset.vibe;
        const status = document.getElementById('room-vibe-status');
        if (status) status.textContent = `Showing rooms with ${pill.textContent.trim().toLowerCase()}.`;
        filterSuites();
      });
    });
  });
</script>